WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.334 --> 00:00:13.939
Tom and Becky had lost track of time.

2
00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:17.580
Their candles had gone out, and they both had fallen asleep.

3
00:00:17.581 --> 00:00:22.389
Had they slept long? Tom wondered. There was no way of knowing.

4
00:00:22.390 --> 00:00:25.811
"I'm so hungry," said Becky.

5
00:00:25.812 --> 00:00:32.802
"Here." Tom passed her some cake. "I saved this for you."

6
00:00:32.803 --> 00:00:36.433
"Are people looking for us?" asked Becky.

7
00:00:36.434 --> 00:00:38.858
"Sure," said Tom.

8
00:00:38.859 --> 00:00:44.932
But he knew the cave was big, and if he and Becky waited to be found, they might wait forever.

9
00:00:44.933 --> 00:00:48.218
"I think I should explore," he said.

10
00:00:48.219 --> 00:00:52.132
"Here, hold one end of this kite string.

11
00:00:52.133 --> 00:00:58.262
I will go down these side passages as far as I can, and then I'll come back."

12
00:00:58.263 --> 00:01:01.945
Becky was scared, but she agreed to Tom's plan.

13
00:01:01.946 --> 00:01:06.484
Tom crawled slowly into the dark, feeling in front of him like a blind man.

14
00:01:06.485 --> 00:01:09.866
He had only gone a short distance when he heard something.

15
00:01:09.867 --> 00:01:15.169
He gave a shout, and his voice echoed eerily throughout the cave.

16
00:01:15.170 --> 00:01:17.048
Then a light appeared.

17
00:01:17.049 --> 00:01:21.456
When Tom saw who was holding the light, he almost shouted again.

18
00:01:21.457 --> 00:01:24.259
The face in the light was Injun Joe's!

19
00:01:24.260 --> 00:01:31.608
Injun Joe looked just as scared to see Tom. He bolted away from him.

20
00:01:31.609 --> 00:01:36.071
When Tom crawled back to Becky, she asked him why he had shouted.

21
00:01:36.072 --> 00:01:38.758
"Just for luck," said Tom.

22
00:01:38.759 --> 00:01:42.618
He didn't want to make Becky more afraid than she already was.

23
00:01:42.619 --> 00:01:47.984
Then he said, "I think I can find a way out, but I need some more luck."

24
00:01:47.985 --> 00:01:50.324
He leaned forward and kissed Becky.

25
00:01:50.325 --> 00:01:55.367
Then he crawled down a different passage.

26
00:01:55.368 --> 00:01:59.829
Kissing Becky had indeed brought Tom some luck.

27
00:01:59.830 --> 00:02:08.412
Soon Tom saw light again, but this was a different kind of light—sunlight shining through a small hole.

28
00:02:08.413 --> 00:02:14.602
Tom took out his knife and gradually made the hole big enough to squeeze through.

29
00:02:14.603 --> 00:02:19.612
After Tom and Becky climbed out of the cave, Tom covered the hole with some leaves.

30
00:02:19.613 --> 00:02:23.614
He didn't want Injun Joe to find it and escape the same way.

31
00:02:23.615 --> 00:02:30.873
When Tom realized where they were, he exclaimed, "Gosh, we're five miles downriver from town!

32
00:02:30.874 --> 00:02:34.929
We walked almost two miles underground."

33
00:02:34.930 --> 00:02:40.618
Tom and Becky walked to the river and got a barge that was headed upriver to stop for them.

34
00:02:40.619 --> 00:02:45.575
The crew on the barge had heard about the missing children, so they agreed to take them home.

35
00:02:45.576 --> 00:02:49.180
The town rejoiced, and then the two children were put to bed.

36
00:02:49.181 --> 00:02:54.473
Becky stayed in bed for almost four days, but Tom felt better after two.

37
00:02:54.474 --> 00:03:00.736
Tom learned that Huck had been sick as well, so Tom went to visit his friend at the Welshman's house.

38
00:03:00.737 --> 00:03:06.467
When Tom and Huck were alone, Tom told Huck that he thought he knew where the treasure was.

39
00:03:06.468 --> 00:03:10.327
Huck shook his head and said, "It isn't in the tavern, Tom."

40
00:03:10.328 --> 00:03:14.644
Tom wanted to interrupt his friend, but Huck was talking too fast.

41
00:03:14.645 --> 00:03:20.485
"When I was sick," said Huck, "I dreamed a lot, and I guess I did a lot of talking.

42
00:03:20.486 --> 00:03:26.320
I talked about the tavern, I talked about Injun Joe and the murder, and I talked about the Widow Douglas.

43
00:03:26.321 --> 00:03:29.606
The Welshman and others figured things out and searched the tavern.

44
00:03:29.607 --> 00:03:32.075
But all they found was whiskey."

45
00:03:32.076 --> 00:03:35.034
Tom smiled. "Of course!

46
00:03:35.035 --> 00:03:38.293
That's all they found because the gold is in the cave.

47
00:03:38.294 --> 00:03:41.814
I saw Injun Joe in the cave."

48
00:03:41.815 --> 00:03:47.176
"The night you were found, Judge Thatcher blocked the cave entrance with an iron door," said Huck.

49
00:03:47.177 --> 00:03:50.710
"He didn't want what happened to you and Becky to happen again."

50
00:03:50.711 --> 00:03:53.383
Tom wanted to go to the judge.

51
00:03:53.384 --> 00:03:58.703
But the Widow Douglas, who had been taking care of Huck at the Welshman's house, wouldn't let Huck go.

52
00:03:58.704 --> 00:04:03.634
So Tom went by himself, and then headed back to the cave with the judge and the sheriff.

53
00:04:03.635 --> 00:04:06.682
The judge opened the great iron door with his key.

54
00:04:06.683 --> 00:04:11.402
Inside they found Injun Joe lying dead on the ground.

55
00:04:11.403 --> 00:04:16.205
His knife was broken at his side where he had tried to chip his way out.

56
00:04:16.206 --> 00:04:22.003
The next day Tom got Huck. They borrowed a rowboat, and Tom rowed downriver.

57
00:04:22.004 --> 00:04:25.127
Tom found his secret entrance to the cave easily.

58
00:04:25.128 --> 00:04:29.212
They each lit a candle and entered.

59
00:04:29.213 --> 00:04:34.924
Tom showed Huck where he and Becky had slept, and then he led Huck to where he had seen Injun Joe.

60
00:04:34.925 --> 00:04:37.264
They climbed down into the chamber.

61
00:04:37.265 --> 00:04:42.443
Tom and Huck both noticed the large cross on the wall, and they immediately started digging.

62
00:04:42.444 --> 00:04:46.900
They didn't have to dig long before they came to a board.

63
00:04:46.901 --> 00:04:50.853
They lifted the board, and under it was a small compartment.

64
00:04:50.854 --> 00:04:57.219
Inside the compartment were some candles, some matches, and a box full of silver and gold.

65
00:04:57.220 --> 00:05:01.662
"Finally!" exclaimed Huck. "We found the treasure!"

66
00:05:01.663 --> 00:05:08.232
"Even when money's free," said Tom, "you still have to work for it."
